      ":question/problem": "Let $a = ⟨2,-3⟩$ and $b = ⟨-1,-4⟩$. Find $4a - 3b$.",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard",
      ":question/worked-solution": "To compute $4a - 3b$, we just need to perform the required operations with each component separately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n4a - 3b &= 4\\cdot ⟨2,-3⟩ - 3\\cdot ⟨-1,-4⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨8,-12⟩ - ⟨-3,-12⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨8 - (-3), -12 - (-12)⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨11,0⟩\n\\end{aligned}\n$$",
